realm-core 20.1.0, src/external/s2/base/macros.h (s2 by Google, Apache License 2.0): the macros DECLARE_POD and
PROPAGATE_POD_FROM_TEMPLATE_ARGUMENT no longer specialize std::is_pod, which the libc++ of Xcode 26.6 rejects
(error: 'is_pod' cannot be specialized, -Winvalid-specialization; the error reported in realm/realm-js#7115). Same
change as the one afterdb ships in the xcframework headers (bridge/build.mjs step 5), plus a comment that marks the
file as changed.
Modified by Pomwik (Firas Hmedi), 2026. Apache License 2.0, like the file it changes.

